 So I think we just spot everything we saw in the previous picture we saw over here.

664
00:48:52,000 --> 00:48:57,000
 So now let's talk a little bit more about the pelvic structure and childbearing.

665
00:48:57,000 --> 00:49:01,000
 So notice that I said in the previous picture that, you know,

666
00:49:01,000 --> 00:49:05,000
 by looking at the pubis, you know, you're able to differentiate

667
00:49:05,000 --> 00:49:10,000
 if it's a male or a female, and in addition to that also how many children,

668
00:49:10,000 --> 00:49:14,000
 if it is a female, how many children this individual may have had.

669
00:49:14,000 --> 00:49:18,000
 Now the pelvis is formed by your hip bone, sacrum, and caustics.

670
00:49:18,000 --> 00:49:23,000
 Having said that, there are still differences between a male and a female pelvis.

671
00:49:23,000 --> 00:49:27,000
 The female pelvis, it's modified for childbearing.

672
00:49:27,000 --> 00:49:31,000
 So it tends to be wider, shallower, lighter, and rounder than that of the male.

673
00:49:31,000 --> 00:49:36,000
 Now the female pelvis not only doesn't need to accommodate the fetus to grow,

674
00:49:36,000 --> 00:49:44,000
 but it also needs to be able to be large enough to allow for the delivery of the child during child birth.

675
00:49:44,000 --> 00:49:48,000
 Now the pelvis is set to consist of a false pelvis and a true pelvis,

676
00:49:48,000 --> 00:49:50,000
 that's separated by a pelvic brim.

677
00:49:50,000 --> 00:49:54,000
 The pelvic brim is a continuous oval ridge that runs from the pubic crest

678
00:49:54,000 --> 00:49:57,000
 through the arcuate lines and sacral promontory.

679
00:49:57,000 --> 00:50:00,000
 Now the false pelvis, this is the portion that's superior to the pelvic brim.

680
00:50:00,000 --> 00:50:05,000
 It's bonded by the ayla of the ilea laterally and the lumbar vertebrae posteriorly.

681
00:50:05,000 --> 00:50:10,000
 Now the false pelvis is really part of the abdomen and it helps support the abdominal viscera

682
00:50:10,000 --> 00:50:13,000
 and it doesn't restrict child birth in any way.

683
00:50:13,000 --> 00:50:19,000
 Now the true pelvis, this is the region inferior to the pelvic brim that's almost entirely surrounded by bone.

684
00:50:19,000 --> 00:50:22,000
 It forms a deep bowl containing the pelvic organs.

685
00:50:22,000 --> 00:50:25,000
 Its dimensions, particularly those of its inlets and alkylids,

686
00:50:25,000 --> 00:50:28,000
 they're very important for delivery of a baby.

687
00:50:28,000 --> 00:50:34,000
 So when a woman is going to the obstetrician for the checkups every so often,

688
00:50:34,000 --> 00:50:40,000
 and especially during the ultrasounds, these are going to be measured

689
00:50:40,000 --> 00:50:45,000
 to make sure that it's large enough to accommodate the child during labor,

690
00:50:45,000 --> 00:50:47,000
 during the delivery process.

691
00:50:47,000 --> 00:50:53,000
 If the doctor suspects that it's not adequate enough for delivery,

692
00:50:53,000 --> 00:51:02,000
 then at that point they'll probably decide to deliver the baby by caesarean section.

693
00:51:02,000 --> 00:51:08,000
 Now the pelvic inlet is the pelvic brim and its widest dimension is from right to left

694
00:51:08,000 --> 00:51:14,000
 along the frontal plane and the pelvic outlet, this is the inferior margin of the true pelvis.

695
00:51:14,000 --> 00:51:18,000
 Now it's bounded anterior to the pubic arch and laterally by the isha

696
00:51:18,000 --> 00:51:22,000
 and posteriorly by the sacrum and caustic.

697
00:51:22,000 --> 00:51:26,000
 Now both caustics and ishaal spines, they protrude into the outlet's opening.

698
00:51:26,000 --> 00:51:31,000
 So a sharply angled caesarean or an unusually large spines,

699
00:51:31,000 --> 00:51:33,000
 they're going to interfere with delivery.

700
00:51:33,000 --> 00:51:37,000
 Now the largest dimension of the outlet is the anterior posterior diameter.

701
00:51:37,000 --> 00:51:42,000
 So generally what happens during childbirth is that the baby's head, it passes through the inlet.

702
00:51:42,000 --> 00:51:47,000
 It rotates so the forehead faces posteriorly and the occiparate anteriorly

703
00:51:47,000 --> 00:51:51,000
 and this is a usual position of the baby's head as it leaves

704
00:51:51,000 --> 00:51:53,000
 the mother's body.

705
00:51:53,000 --> 00:51:58,000
 So during birth, the infant's head, it makes a quarter turn to follow the widest dimension

706
00:51:58,000 --> 00:52:00,000
 of the true pelvis.

707
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:05,000
 So this chart over here, it goes over and distinguishes some of the characteristics

708
00:52:05,000 --> 00:52:10,000
 between a female and a male pelvic bones.

709
00:52:10,000 --> 00:52:15,000
 So again, let's go through this and discuss this a little bit.

710
00:52:15,000 --> 00:52:20,000
 So as far as bone thickness goes, in females,

711
00:52:20,000 --> 00:52:28,000
 it's going to be lighter, less thick and it's going to be much more smoother.

712
00:52:28,000 --> 00:52:33,000
 Now in men's, again, it's going to be heavier, it's going to be thicker

713
00:52:33,000 --> 00:52:35,000
 and you're going to have a lot more prominent marking.

714
00:52:35,000 --> 00:52:36,000
 Why is that the case?

715
00:52:36,000 --> 00:52:41,000
 Well, men have bigger and larger muscles than female do, generally speaking.

716
00:52:41,000 --> 00:52:42,000
 So this is why.

717
00:52:42,000 --> 00:52:52,000
 Now, in addition to that, as far as the acetabular go, they're farther apart.

718
00:52:52,000 --> 00:52:57,000
 Okay, why? Because again, you have much, the wings over here, they're far more,

719
00:52:57,000 --> 00:52:59,000
 they're flared out, it's much more wider.

720
00:52:59,000 --> 00:53:02,000
 So if you look over here, look at this pelvic brain.

721
00:53:02,000 --> 00:53:04,000
 Look how much wider this is.

722
00:53:04,000 --> 00:53:08,000
 And when you look at the shape over here, it's almost like an oval shape in the female.

723
00:53:08,000 --> 00:53:12,000
 Now when you look at the male, this is more of a heart shaped.

724
00:53:12,000 --> 00:53:15,000
 So if you were, you know, if you were to get a hip and you look at it and you kind of see

725
00:53:15,000 --> 00:53:20,000
 like this heart shaped form over here, that's a pretty good indication that it's probably a male.

726
00:53:20,000 --> 00:53:22,000
 But that should not be the only criteria.

727
00:53:22,000 --> 00:53:28,000
 Again, in the female when you look at it, it's going to look a little more like an oval shaped.

728
00:53:28,000 --> 00:53:34,000
 So again, the acetabular farther apart in the males, they're going to be closer.

729
00:53:34,000 --> 00:53:37,000
 Also, we look at this pubic arch.

730
00:53:37,000 --> 00:53:41,000
 In the female, you have this very broad angle that forms over here.

731
00:53:41,000 --> 00:53:46,000
 So it's more than 90 degrees, anywhere from between 80 to 90 degrees and beyond.

732
00:53:46,000 --> 00:53:47,000
 So look how wide this is.

733
00:53:47,000 --> 00:53:56,000
 And when you look at the male pelvis here, the pubic or the sub pubic angle, it's very narrow.

734
00:53:56,000 --> 00:53:58,000
 Okay, right over here, look how narrow this is.

735
00:53:58,000 --> 00:54:00,000
 So it's, you're going to see a cute angle over here.

736
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:06,000
 So anywhere between 45, 50 to 60 degrees, usually, this is what you'll find.

737
00:54:06,000 --> 00:54:12,000
 So in males also, it's tilted less forward.

738
00:54:12,000 --> 00:54:14,000
 We're in females, it's tilted forward.

739
00:54:14,000 --> 00:54:19,000
 And again, remember, this bone is adapted for childbearing.

740
00:54:19,000 --> 00:54:29,000
 And this type of pelvis bone, it's not adapted for childbearing, but it's made to, you know, to accommodate more weight.

741
00:54:29,000 --> 00:54:37,000
 As a, you know, think of it this way, men, they have a lot more muscle, they have a heavier build.

742
00:54:37,000 --> 00:54:44,000
 So they need to have a lot more muscles and they need to have a much more, again, a stapler, narrower form.

743
00:54:44,000 --> 00:54:46,000
 So this is why they're going to get this.

744
00:54:46,000 --> 00:54:52,000
 It's how the body is designed between male and females that these structures are different also.

745
00:54:52,000 --> 00:55:00,000
 Remember, structure and function over and over again, we've been seeing this and now, you know, you can see that at this level as well.

746
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:05,000
 This is a photograph also, and you can see the two over here.

